I'll inspect the client project before touching anything — the request is about the **new session settings** of the browser session manager UI.I have everything I need: the browser UI lives in `src/components/browsers/` + `src/store/browsers.js`, and project folders can be listed through `$api.files.list()` (`{ files: [{ name, is_dir, file_path }] }`).

**Objective**
- Turn the sidebar *New Session* form into real session settings: project-folder mapping (`share_project` / `share_folders` / `readonly`), a downloads folder and the container path preview (`/home/<project>/…`).
- Add a project folder picker (multi + single mode) built on the existing files API.
- Forward the settings on create, and surface the mapping of a running session.

**Changes summary**

| File | Change |
|---|---|
| `src/components/browsers/BrowserFolderPicker.vue` | **new** modal folder picker (multi/single, breadcrumb, root row) |
| `src/components/browsers/BrowserSessionCreateForm.vue` | **new** session settings form (name, url, mount mode, folders, readonly, downloads) |
| `src/components/browsers/BrowserSessionList.vue` | inline form replaced by the new form + `create` handler |
| `src/store/browsers.js` | `createSession` forwards the mapping fields |
| `src/api/modules/browsers.js` | documented create payload |
| `src/components/browsers/BrowserSessionPanel.vue` | shows the mounted folders/downloads of the selected session |

